SECTION 5: AUDITOR RECOMMENDATION & NEXT STEPS
1. Decision
CONDITIONAL APPROVAL
ENGIE RCS Pte. Ltd. presents a fundamentally sound profile for onboarding as a TPA: it is a legitimate, ACRA-confirmed, actively-trading Singapore construction company with a clean open-source footprint, audited financials from a recognised firm, and a transparent 4-tier corporate structure rooted in a Euronext-listed French multinational. There is no basis for blocking onboarding at this stage.

However, the current record cannot be approved unconditionally given: (a) 8 mandatory onboarding fields remain unfilled due to a specimen-only contract; (b) RCTP screening results for all 6 parties are outstanding; and (c) two compliance officer adjudication items (listed-entity exemption; French State voting rights) have not been formally resolved.

2. Conditions for Full Approval
The following conditions must all be satisfied before APPROVED FOR ONBOARDING status can be issued:

#	Condition	Owner	Deadline
C1	Executed Contract Agreement / LOA naming ENGIE RCS as Contractor submitted and reviewed	Requester + OpsManager	30 July 2026
C2	All 8 outstanding mandatory TPA Risk Assessment fields completed (CEO name, commercial justification, RF flags, payment terms, contract sum, third-party interaction)	Requester	30 July 2026
C3	RCTP results received, adjudicated, and all 6 parties cleared (no unresolved true matches)	Senior Compliance Officer	Within 3 business days of RCTP receipt
C4	Listed-entity UBO exemption for ENGIE S.A. formally adjudicated and recorded in writing	Senior Compliance Officer	23 July 2026
C5	French State voting-rights position assessed and compliance determination recorded	Senior Compliance Officer	23 July 2026
C6	ACRA Bizfile for ENGIE South East Asia Pte. Ltd. obtained and filed	TPA Onboarding Team	30 July 2026
C7	Indonesian representative office EDD assessment completed	Senior Compliance Officer	6 August 2026
3. Escalation Path
If any RCTP result returns a TRUE MATCH on any sanctioned list or confirmed PEP designation: → Immediate escalation to Senior Compliance Officer and Group Legal. Onboarding halted. Status reclassified to 🔴 CRITICAL. No contractual commitment to proceed until cleared.

If the French State sovereign ownership assessment triggers additional due diligence requirements under institutional policy: → Escalate to Chief Compliance Officer for written policy determination.

If C1 (executed contract) is not received by 30 July 2026: → Onboarding file to be placed on administrative hold. Requester to be notified that TPA cannot be registered in the portfolio without an executed instrument.

4. Next Review Date
Conditional milestone review: No later than August 13, 2026 — by which time all C1–C7 conditions above should be resolved or a clear disposition recorded. If all conditions are satisfied prior to that date, onboarding file may be closed and TPA registered in app:portfolio_registry at that earlier date.

Standard periodic review (once onboarded): Per portfolio-sweep cycle — 12 months post-onboarding, unless contract term or risk tier warrants earlier review.

